# Roadmap

Broad steps left. Order is a suggestion, not a commitment.

## Foundations
- [ ] Icons as a system: size scale usage, stroke width, optical alignment with text, how icons sit inside Button, Link, Menu items, Select, Input, Badge, Alert, Tabs. One docs page + one rule set.
- [ ] Borders: when to use `border-default|subtle|strong`, border vs `--shadow-border`, border width tokens.
- [ ] Shape: radius scale and usage per component.
- [ ] Spacing: scale, gap/padding rules, density.
- [ ] Motion: durations, easings, reduced-motion, press/hover/enter/exit patterns.
- [ ] Docs pages for breakpoints and the icon scale.

## Components
- [ ] Pass over every component against the new color, typography and shadow tokens (migration prompts delivered; verify applied).
- [ ] Icon alignment inside Menu, Link, Select, Tabs, Badge (same `data-icon` idea as Button).
- [ ] `Text` `italic` prop (needs `dm-sans/opsz-italic.css`).
- [ ] Missing components: Combobox/Autocomplete, DatePicker, Command palette, Sheet/Drawer, Toggle/ToggleGroup, Tag/Chip, Empty state.
- [ ] Forms: validation states, error/help text patterns, form-level composition.

## Library
- [ ] Compatibility: test with Vite and Astro, React 17-19; then update Installation "Requirements".
- [ ] Packaging: exports, types, CSS entry points, tree-shaking, versioning and changelog.
- [ ] Tailwind output (`tailwind.css`) validated in a real Tailwind project.
- [ ] Theming guide: how consumers override tokens and create their own theme.

## Docs site
- [ ] Brand: logo SVGs, favicon, name (Javui).
- [ ] Getting started, Installation, Theming, Accessibility pages.
- [ ] Per-component examples with live playground and copyable code.
- [ ] Search palette polish; mobile pass of the whole site.

## Agent layer
- [ ] Keep `agent-meta.json`, manifest and MCP in sync with new tokens and components; fix `mcp:test` primitives check.
- [ ] Prompts/recipes for agents: build a page, migrate a theme, add a component.

## Quality
- [ ] Visual regression screenshots (light/dark, mobile/desktop).
- [ ] Full a11y audit (keyboard, screen reader, contrast of every token pair).
- [ ] CI: typecheck, lint, test, build, storybook tests.

## Release
- [ ] Publish to npm, license, contributing guide, public docs domain.